  3352	# v9 OPENING: a cash-safe step-0 wheat trade.
  3353	#
  3354	# Every route tape opens with a wheat round trip
  3355	#     step 0: BUY 13, BUY 30, SELL 30      step 1: SELL 13, BUY 5   (net +5)
  3356	# and then runs days 0-9 with only ~$6 of cash slack (minimum at step 32).
  3357	# The round trip wins cash from rivals whose own opening buys into it, but
  3358	# against openings that dump wheat in the same slots (e.g. BUY 43 / SELL 20 /
  3359	# SELL 22 or BUY 30 / SELL all) it ends step 1 up to $75 short; the day-1
  3360	# wheat and hire orders then fail, the herd goes unfed, and by days 5-8 the
  3361	# strawberry seed orders fail too (18-21 plants instead of 33, -20k..-65k).
  3362	#
  3363	# Replacing it with BUY 10, SELL 5 at step 0 (still net +5, nothing at
  3364	# step 1) leaves >= $1,050 after step 1 against all 6,648 recorded openings
  3365	# in the metav2 / M&M replays (exact market simulation, build/v9/opensim.py),
  3366	# and $2 more than the round trip against the V38/V39 tape lineage.
